1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,655
Unless you work in a very small company,

2
00:00:02,655 --> 00:00:07,540
you most likely be working with a lot of partners including product marketing manager.

3
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:11,145
What is the difference between PM and a PMM?

4
00:00:11,145 --> 00:00:15,045
In some companies, there isn't a true separation between the two,

5
00:00:15,045 --> 00:00:19,740
but in general, the PM is responsible for developing the product vision,

6
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:22,620
defining the key features of the product,

7
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:27,210
working with all the teams needed to create a product that meets that vision,

8
00:00:27,210 --> 00:00:30,750
and managing the timeline of product development and release.

9
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:34,080
The PMM is responsible for communicating that vision to

10
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:39,540
users and getting them excited about the product the team has created.

11
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:43,445
They typically work closely with the product manager and sales team,

12
00:00:43,445 --> 00:00:46,115
and manage the implementation of the pricing,

13
00:00:46,115 --> 00:00:48,620
messaging, and channel strategies.

14
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:55,510
In general, the PM owns the product and the PMM owns the go-to-market strategy.

15
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:59,940
While the product marketing manager owns the implementation of the go-to-market strategy,

16
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:04,250
the PM and the product marketing manager need to collaborate to develop it.

17
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:07,430
We'll learn more about the process in a little bit.

18
00:01:07,430 --> 00:01:09,680
You should involve your marketing partner in

19
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:12,110
the product development as early as possible,

20
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:13,655
and why should you do that?

21
00:01:13,655 --> 00:01:17,690
Well, your marketing partner will need to think about how to market your product,

22
00:01:17,690 --> 00:01:20,485
it is better to start thinking about it early on,

23
00:01:20,485 --> 00:01:24,300
plus marketing partners have a lot of insight into the market,

24
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:27,425
so they can help you validate the ideas early on.

25
00:01:27,425 --> 00:01:32,680
Not to mention, they can help you think through how to acquire users.

26
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:37,970
For example, if you're planning to acquire users for promotions or similar channels,

27
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:40,520
your marketing can guide you and help you think through

28
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:45,655
these channels and actually start on creating promotions marketing materials.

29
00:01:45,655 --> 00:01:51,080
Your role will be to make sure that marketing partners are working in sync review,

30
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:54,440
so they in turn can create a comprehensive marketing strategy.

31
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:59,315
A good marketing strategy will help your product to gain the attention of your users.

32
00:01:59,315 --> 00:02:03,480
So how do you achieve great collaboration with your marketing partner?

33
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:06,390
The same way we discussed in the previous lesson.

34
00:02:06,390 --> 00:02:12,290
Communication. Part of it is also to have constant communication and not one-off.

35
00:02:12,290 --> 00:02:17,170
I personally like having set time to meet with my marketing partner.

36
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:20,240
During this meeting, we discuss all our projects,

37
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,310
we look at the road map,

38
00:02:21,310 --> 00:02:24,985
the planning and follow-ups on all our running projects.

39
00:02:24,985 --> 00:02:28,865
Having good personal relationship helps move things forward.

40
00:02:28,865 --> 00:02:31,355
More than once, we share the important information

41
00:02:31,355 --> 00:02:34,645
just because it was in our mindset to update each other,

42
00:02:34,645 --> 00:02:38,670
this also allows us good planning for the future.

